<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>AVideoRouter — Zoom & Fathom recordings, auto-published to YouTube and your LMS</title>
  <meta name="description" content="VideoRouter automatically routes your Zoom and Fathom recordings to YouTube and your course platform — on a schedule, hands-free. Pay as you go, first upload free.">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://avr.divineleads.guru/">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": "https://avr.divineleads.guru/#org",
        "name": "AVideoRouter",
        "url": "https://avr.divineleads.guru/",
        "email": "connect@divineleads.guru",
        "description": "AVideoRouter automatically moves Zoom and Fathom recordings to YouTube and your LMS, on a schedule, hands-free.",
        "parentOrganization": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Divine Leads" }
      },
      {
        "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
        "name": "AVideoRouter",
        "applicationCategory": "BusinessApplication",
        "operatingSystem": "Web",
        "url": "https://avr.divineleads.guru/",
        "description": "Automatically routes Zoom and Fathom recordings to YouTube and your LMS — download, upload, organize and optionally delete the Zoom original — on a schedule, hands-free.",
        "publisher": { "@id": "https://avr.divineleads.guru/#org" },
        "offers": {
          "@type": "Offer",
          "price": "50",
          "priceCurrency": "INR",
          "description": "Pay as you go — ₹50 per GB of actual data transferred (a 2.5 GB file is 2.5 GB, not rounded up). First upload free. Optional Always-On subscription."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
  <%- typeof pixelHead !== 'undefined' ? pixelHead : '' %>
  <style>
    :root{
      --bg:#0f1420; --panel:#1a2233; --panel2:#223048; --line:#2e3d5c;
      --text:#e8edf7; --muted:#93a1bd; --accent:#4f8cff; --accent2:#7b5cff;
      --ok:#2ecc71;
    }
    :root[data-theme="light"]{
      --bg:#f6f8fc; --panel:#ffffff; --panel2:#eef2f8; --line:#d6deea;
      --text:#151a22; --muted:#5b6b84; --accent:#2f68e0; --accent2:#6b4cff; --ok:#1e9e56;
    }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);
      font:16px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
    a{color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none}
    .wrap{max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 28px}
    .btn{display:inline-block;padding:12px 22px;border-radius:8px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--line);
      background:var(--panel2);color:var(--text);cursor:pointer}
    .btn.primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent2));border:none;color:#fff}
    .btn.big{padding:15px 30px;font-size:17px}

    header{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:20;background:rgba(15,20,32,.85);backdrop-filter:blur(8px);
      border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    header .wrap{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;height:62px}
    .brand{font-weight:800;font-size:19px;letter-spacing:.2px}
    .brand span{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent2));-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent}
    .hero-visual{display:flex;justify-content:center;margin:10px auto 0;max-width:840px}
    .hero-img{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.4)}

    .hero{text-align:center;padding:70px 0 40px}
    .hero h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,50px);line-height:1.1;margin:0 0 18px;font-weight:800}
    .hero h1 .hl{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent2));-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent}
    .hero p.sub{font-size:clamp(17px,2.2vw,21px);color:var(--muted);max-width:720px;margin:0 auto 28px}
    .cta-row{display:flex;gap:14px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap}
    .tiny{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;margin-top:14px}

    .video{padding:10px 0 20px}
    .video-frame{position:relative;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;aspect-ratio:16/9;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;
      border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--panel);box-shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.45)}
    .video-frame iframe{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0}

    .speed{margin:24px auto;max-width:900px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(79,140,255,.14),rgba(123,92,255,.14));
      border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:22px 26px;display:flex;gap:26px;align-items:center;
      justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;text-align:center}
    .speed b{font-size:22px}
    .speed .num{font-size:34px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent)}

    section{padding:56px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    section h2{font-size:clamp(24px,3.4vw,34px);margin:0 0 10px;text-align:center;font-weight:800}
    section .lead{color:var(--muted);text-align:center;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto 34px}

    .steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}
    .step{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px}
    .step .n{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--accent),var(--accent2));color:#fff;margin-bottom:12px}
    .step h3{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:18px}
    .step p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}

    .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}
    .feat{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px}
    .feat .ic{font-size:24px;margin-bottom:10px}
    .feat h3{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:17px}
    .feat p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);font-size:15px}
    .cmp-wrap{overflow-x:auto}
    table.cmp{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:760px;font-size:15px}
    table.cmp th,table.cmp td{padding:12px 14px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    table.cmp thead th{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}
    table.cmp tbody th{font-weight:600}
    table.cmp col.uscol,table.cmp th.us,table.cmp td.us{background:var(--panel2)}
    table.cmp thead th.us{color:var(--accent);font-size:15px}
    table.cmp .y{color:var(--ok,#2ea56b);font-weight:700}
    table.cmp .n{color:var(--muted)}
    table.cmp .p{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
    .cmp-note{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;margin-top:14px;text-align:center}

    .price{max-width:520px;margin:0 auto;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;text-align:center}
    .price .amt{font-size:44px;font-weight:800}
    .price .amt small{font-size:17px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:500}
    .price ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:20px 0;text-align:left;display:inline-block}
    .price li{padding:7px 0;color:var(--text)}
    .price li::before{content:"✓";color:var(--ok);font-weight:800;margin-right:10px}
    .price-row{display:flex;gap:22px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch}
    .price-row .price{margin:0;flex:1 1 340px;max-width:420px;text-align:left}
    .price-row .price .amt{text-align:left}
    .price small{color:var(--muted)}
    .price .ptitle{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:19px}
    .price li.excl::before{content:"✗";color:#e0674f}
    .kb-btn{background:#f2b705;color:#14181f;border-color:#f2b705;font-weight:700}
    .kb-btn:hover{background:#ffc21f;border-color:#ffc21f}

    .faq{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto}
    .faq details{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 20px;margin-bottom:12px}
    .faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}
    .faq p{color:var(--muted);margin:10px 0 0}

    .final{text-align:center}
    footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:30px 0;color:var(--muted);text-align:center;font-size:14px}

    /* REALITY-CHECK section (directly below hero) */
    .rc .eyebrow{display:inline-block;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;
      color:var(--accent);background:var(--panel2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:6px 15px;margin-bottom:18px}
    .rc .emph{max-width:840px;margin:28px auto 0;
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(79,140,255,.14),rgba(123,92,255,.14));
      border:1px solid var(--accent);border-radius:14px;padding:22px 26px;text-align:center;
      font-size:clamp(16px,2vw,19px);line-height:1.6}
    .rc .emph b{color:var(--text)}
    .rc-scroll{margin-top:36px}
    table.rc-tbl{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px}
    table.rc-tbl th,table.rc-tbl td{padding:14px 16px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}
    table.rc-tbl thead th{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;white-space:nowrap}
    table.rc-tbl tbody th{font-weight:700;font-size:16px}
    table.rc-tbl .why{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}
    table.rc-tbl .lim{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}
    table.rc-tbl .status{white-space:nowrap;font-weight:700}
    table.rc-tbl .cost .money{display:block;font-weight:600}
    table.rc-tbl .cost .effort{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;margin-top:5px}
    table.rc-tbl .cost a{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}
    table.rc-tbl tr.us th,table.rc-tbl tr.us td{
      background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(79,140,255,.16),rgba(123,92,255,.16));
      border-top:1px solid var(--accent);border-bottom:1px solid var(--accent)}
    table.rc-tbl tr.us th{border-left:3px solid var(--accent)}
    table.rc-tbl tr.us td:last-child{border-right:1px solid var(--accent)}
    .rc-foot{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin-top:20px;text-align:center;max-width:760px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}
    @media(max-width:760px){
      .steps,.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
      table.rc-tbl thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)}
      table.rc-tbl,table.rc-tbl tbody,table.rc-tbl tr,table.rc-tbl th,table.rc-tbl td{display:block;width:100%}
      table.rc-tbl tr{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:16px;overflow:hidden}
      table.rc-tbl tr.us{border-color:var(--accent)}
      table.rc-tbl th,table.rc-tbl td{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:12px 16px}
      table.rc-tbl tr td:last-child{border-bottom:none}
      table.rc-tbl tbody th{font-size:19px;background:var(--panel2);border-bottom:2px solid var(--line)}
      table.rc-tbl tr.us th{background:transparent;border-left:0}
      table.rc-tbl tr.us th,table.rc-tbl tr.us td{border-top:0}
      table.rc-tbl tr.us td:last-child{border-right:0}
      table.rc-tbl td::before{content:attr(data-label);display:block;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.05em;
        text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:5px}
    }
  </style>
  <script src="/public/theme.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header><div class="wrap">
    <div class="brand"><span>A</span>Video<span>Router</span></div>
    <span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px"><span data-theme-toggle></span><a class="btn primary" href="/register">Sign up free</a><a class="btn" href="/login">Log in</a></span>
  </div></header>

  <div class="wrap">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>Your Zoom &amp; Fathom recordings — auto-published to YouTube <span class="hl">and into your Course LMS</span></h1>
      <p class="sub">Most tools stop at YouTube. AVideoRouter also files every recording into the right
        LMS course and module, then clears it off Zoom. Connect once, set your rules, and it runs —
        on a schedule or one click.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn primary big" href="/register">Start free — first upload's on us</a>
        <a class="btn big" href="#how">See how it works</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tiny">Start free · Pay as you go · GST invoice provided</div>
    </div>

    <!-- HERO VISUAL (the product-story banner) -->
    <div class="hero-visual">
      <img src="/public/logo.jpg" alt="AVideoRouter — Zoom and Fathom recordings routed through AI to YouTube and your LMS"
        class="hero-img" onerror="this.closest('.hero-visual').style.display='none'">
    </div>

    <!-- HERO VIDEO (pulled live from settings — accepts a full embed snippet OR a bare URL) -->
    <% if (videoUrl) { %>
      <% if (/^\s*</.test(videoUrl)) { %>
        <div class="video"><%- videoUrl %></div>
      <% } else { %>
        <div class="video"><div class="video-frame">
          <iframe src="<%= videoUrl %>" title="AVideoRouter demo" loading="lazy"
            allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; encrypted-media" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div></div>
      <% } %>
    <% } %>

    <!-- SPEED / JAW-DROP -->
    <div class="speed">
      <div><div class="num">~90 sec</div><div class="muted">for a full 1&nbsp;GB video</div></div>
      <div style="text-align:left">
        <b>Built for 2–4&nbsp;GB class recordings.</b><br>
        <span class="muted">≈ 60 seconds to download from the source, ≈ 30 seconds to upload. And because we
        <b>stream</b> the whole file — instead of handing a URL to YouTube — the big recordings that break
        other tools go through cleanly.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- REALITY CHECK (directly below hero) -->
  <section class="rc">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
      <span class="eyebrow">The part the tutorials skip</span>
      <h2>The workflow works. Until the file gets real.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Anyone can wire Zoom → YouTube in n8n, Make, or Pabbly. The demo runs on a 40&nbsp;MB clip
        and everyone claps. Then you feed it an actual 2–4&nbsp;GB recording — and it dies. So you're back to
        downloading each session, waiting, and re-uploading by hand. Every single time.</p>
      <p class="emph"><b>AVideoRouter streams the file instead of swallowing it</b> — so 2–4&nbsp;GB+ recordings move
        Zoom/Fathom → YouTube or your LMS reliably, hands-off, in real time. <b>No caps. No crashes. No manual re-uploads.</b></p>

      <div class="rc-scroll">
        <table class="rc-tbl">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Tool</th>
              <th>Max limit</th>
              <th>2–4&nbsp;GB recording?</th>
              <th>Why it breaks</th>
              <th>Real cost</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Make</th>
              <td class="lim" data-label="Max limit">Total data transfer capped per month — Make's own limits: 100&nbsp;MB (Free), 1&nbsp;GB (Core), 10&nbsp;GB (Pro/Teams).</td>
              <td class="status" data-label="2–4 GB recording?">❌ Fails</td>
              <td class="why" data-label="Why it breaks">Hard monthly transfer cap. One 3&nbsp;GB recording eats a third of the Pro plan; a few files and you're locked out for the month.</td>
              <td class="cost" data-label="Real cost">
                <span class="money">💰 ~$16–19/mo</span>
                <span class="effort">⏱ Hours to build, then it fails on the first real file</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Pabbly</th>
              <td class="lim" data-label="Max limit">No published large-file support. A coach put it plainly: “I tried pushing a 2.3&nbsp;GB Zoom recording through Pabbly — it just choked. It's built for form and CRM data, not video.”</td>
              <td class="status" data-label="2–4 GB recording?">❌ Fails</td>
              <td class="why" data-label="Why it breaks">Never designed to carry video — there's no multi-GB path to use.</td>
              <td class="cost" data-label="Real cost">
                <span class="money">💰 ~$16/mo (or ~$349 lifetime)</span>
                <span class="effort">⏱ Quick to wire up — straight into a dead end</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">n8n (self-hosted)</th>
              <td class="lim" data-label="Max limit">No hard cap, but a hard memory wall. n8n's own docs say binary data is held in memory by default and “can cause crashes when working with large files.” A coach's real run: “My 3&nbsp;GB upload crashed with out-of-memory — even after I switched to filesystem mode. The node still loads the whole file to send it.”</td>
              <td class="status" data-label="2–4 GB recording?">⚠️ Fails on any normal host</td>
              <td class="why" data-label="Why it breaks">Loads the entire video into RAM to upload it. Needs 12–16&nbsp;GB of RAM to even attempt a large file — and still fails intermittently.</td>
              <td class="cost" data-label="Real cost">
                <span class="money">💰 $60–160/mo once RAM is sized for video</span>
                <span class="effort">⏱ Days of config + crash-debugging</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Doing it by hand</th>
              <td class="lim" data-label="Max limit">Unlimited — because you are the pipeline.</td>
              <td class="status" data-label="2–4 GB recording?">✅ (but you're the bottleneck)</td>
              <td class="why" data-label="Why it breaks">Nothing breaks except your calendar and the boring task. Download, wait, re-upload — for every recording, forever.</td>
              <td class="cost" data-label="Real cost">
                <span class="money">💰 $0 software</span>
                <span class="effort">⏱ Your time, every single recording, indefinitely, day in and day out.</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="us">
              <th scope="row">AVideoRouter</th>
              <td class="lim" data-label="Max limit">No cap. Streams the file — never loads it into memory.</td>
              <td class="status" data-label="2–4 GB recording?">✅ Works</td>
              <td class="why" data-label="Why it breaks">It doesn't. Real-time, automatic, hands-off.</td>
              <td class="cost" data-label="Real cost">
                <span class="money">💰 <a href="#pricing">See the pricing section below</a></span>
                <span class="effort">⏱ ~Zero — set once, then forget it</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="rc-foot">The “cheap” tools bill you monthly to fail. Doing it by hand is the most expensive of all —
        it just hides the cost in your evenings.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROBLEM -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>The after-class grind, gone</h2>
      <p class="lead">Every recording is 10–20 minutes of the same busywork: download and wait; upload to
        YouTube and set the title and privacy; file it into the right course and module; then clear it off
        Zoom before storage fills. Thirty recordings a month is <b>8–10 hours</b> of it. AVideoRouter does
        the whole chain for you.</p>
      <div class="speed" style="margin-top:28px">
        <span class="muted" style="text-align:left">Unlike general automation tools, AVideoRouter is built for exactly this job:
          it <b>streams large files</b> without choking, and it routes into your <b>LMS course</b> — not just YouTube.
          No scenario-building, no subscription to start, priced in ₹ with a GST invoice.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
  <section id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p class="lead">Set it up once. Then it just runs.</p>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><h3>Connect</h3>
          <p>Link Zoom &amp; Fathom, your YouTube channel(s), and your LMS. One-time, secure.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><h3>Set rules</h3>
          <p>Map each recording to its channel, course and module — with your title and privacy defaults.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><h3>Relax</h3>
          <p>On a schedule or one click, every recording is routed end-to-end and logged.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FEATURES -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Everything you need to publish at scale</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">🎯</div><h3>YouTube <em>and</em> your LMS course</h3>
          <p>The difference: publish to YouTube and file straight into the right LMS course and module. Most tools stop at YouTube.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">🎥</div><h3>Zoom &amp; Fathom sources</h3>
          <p>Recordings are pulled from Zoom and Fathom automatically — no manual downloads.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">⚡</div><h3>Built for big files</h3>
          <p>We stream the whole file, so 2–4&nbsp;GB class recordings upload cleanly where URL-passing tools fail.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">🧹</div><h3>Delete from Zoom, right here</h3>
          <p>Clear published recordings off Zoom from the dashboard — without ever signing in to Zoom.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">🚀</div><h3>Zoom &amp; Fathom fast transfer</h3>
          <p><b>1&nbsp;GB in under 90&nbsp;seconds</b>, source to YouTube — fast enough to clear a full week of recordings in minutes.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">👀</div><h3>Preview &amp; label before you publish</h3>
          <p>Play any recording right in the dashboard and pick the exact view, then set its <b>title and description</b> before it goes to YouTube.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">🔀</div><h3>Push to YouTube &amp; LMS separately</h3>
          <p>Upload to YouTube now, and file it into a course whenever you're ready — two one-click actions, on your timing.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">⏱️</div><h3>Daily scheduler <small class="muted">· Always-On</small></h3>
          <p>Regular sessions? Run batches on a daily schedule, hands-free, and watch every step in the logs.</p></div>
        <div class="feat"><div class="ic">👥</div><h3>Team seats <small class="muted">· Always-On</small></h3>
          <p>Add your team with view or edit access — so simple anyone can run it.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COMPARISON -->
  <section id="compare">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How AVideoRouter compares</h2>
      <p class="lead">General automation tools stop at YouTube, choke on big class recordings, and bill you every month. Single-purpose apps skip your LMS entirely. AVideoRouter does the whole job — connect once, no building.</p>
      <div class="cmp-wrap">
        <table class="cmp">
          <colgroup><col><col class="uscol"><col><col><col><col></colgroup>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Capability</th>
              <th class="us">AVideoRouter</th>
              <th>Xapier</th>
              <th>Maik</th>
              <th>m8m</th>
